# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# ESD K9 Cooper - environment variables
#
# Copy this file to `.env.local` for local development, and add the same
# variables in the Vercel dashboard for production.
#
# NOTHING SECRET GOES IN A NEXT_PUBLIC_ VARIABLE. Anything prefixed with
# NEXT_PUBLIC_ is embedded in the JavaScript sent to every visitor's browser.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# The site's canonical origin. Used for canonical URLs, the sitemap, robots.txt
# and social share cards. No trailing slash.
# Set this in Vercel to your real domain before launch.
NEXT_PUBLIC_SITE_URL=http://localhost:3000


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# OPTIONAL - analytics
#
# The site ships with analytics OFF. Leave everything below unset and no
# third-party script loads and no request leaves the visitor's browser.
#
# The chosen provider is Cloudflare Web Analytics: free, cookieless, and no
# consent banner needed. See docs/ANALYTICS.md.
#
# YOU LIKELY DO NOT NEED THE VARIABLE BELOW. Because Cloudflare serves this
# site, it can inject the beacon itself from the dashboard with no code and no
# rebuild. Only set a token here if you have deliberately turned that automatic
# injection OFF - running both double-counts every visit.
#
# The site is a static export, so this is baked in at BUILD time. Setting it
# locally only affects local builds; for the live site set it in
# Cloudflare -> Workers & Pages -> k9cooper-com -> Settings -> Build -> Variables.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# NEXT_PUBLIC_CF_BEACON_TOKEN=

# If you ever move to a provider that records custom events - Cloudflare Web
# Analytics does not - src/lib/analytics.ts already speaks Plausible, Umami,
# Fathom and gtag. Add its script in src/app/layout.tsx and the twelve events
# already wired across the site start reporting on their own.


# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# NOT USED TODAY - kept as a reference for future work
#
# The contact page currently opens the visitor's own email client and sends
# nothing to a server, so no mail provider key is needed. If a real server-side
# form is added later (see the comment block in
# src/components/contact/ContactForm.tsx), the provider key goes here WITHOUT
# the NEXT_PUBLIC_ prefix so it stays server-only.
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------

# CONTACT_MAIL_API_KEY=
# CONTACT_MAIL_FROM=
